From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Guido=20G=C3=BCnther?= <agx@sigxcpu.org>
Date: Tue, 20 May 2025 10:31:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] broadband-modem-qmi/cellbroadcast: Return on failure
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Return after setting the error

Fixes: e25dd7db9 ("broadband-modem-qmi: Add support for loading channels")

Signed-off-by: Guido Günther <agx@sigxcpu.org>
(cherry picked from commit f17430b662e972fa18ff5b4929394959e47c1afe)
---
 src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c b/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
index 599481e7..0c171cfc 100644
--- a/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
+++ b/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
@@ -11218,6 +11218,7 @@ cell_broadcast_get_broadcast_config_ready (QmiClientWms *client,
             g_error_new (MM_CORE_ERROR, MM_CORE_ERROR_FAILED,
                          "Couldn't parse channel interval '%d-%d'", elem.start, elem.end);
             g_task_return_error (task, error);
+            return;
         }
 
         ch.start = elem.start;
